<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia employment rises 11,900 in June.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia employment rises 11,900 in June.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's seasonally adjusted estimate of the number of employed persons rose 11,900 in June to 8.392 million, against 8.380 million in May and 8.331 million a year earlier, the Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted unemployment rate fell to 8.5 percent from 8.8 percent in May, compared with 8.3 percent in June 1996. Full-time employment fell around 16,900, while part-time rose 28,800.</p>
<p>Economists had on average expected employment to rise around 40,250 in June, with the unemployment rate easing to 8.7 percent.  </p>
<p>AUSTRALIAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>    (Seasonally adj)     June  97     May  97     June  96</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate     8.5 pct     8.8 pct	8.3 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		 8.39 million    8.38 million     8.33 million</p>
<p>    Unemployed		777,800     809,800	757,100</p>
<p>    Participation Rate   63.0 pct    63.2 pct     63.4 pct</p>
<p>(Unadjusted)</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate     8.2 pct     8.6 pct	8.0 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		 8.42 million    8.39 million     8.35 million</p>
<p>    Unemployed		750,800     791,900	730,500</p>
<p>    Participation Rate   63.0 pct    63.1 pct     63.3 pct</p>
<p>(Trend Estimates)</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate    8.7 pct	8.7 pct	8.6 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		8.39 million     8.40 million     8.33 million</p>
<p>    Unemployed	     796,500	799,800	781,300</p>
<p>    Participation Rate  63.1 pct     63.2 pct     63.5 pct</p>
<p>The Bureau said the June unemployment rate was the lowest monthly jobless rate since November 1996, when it was also 8.5 percent.</p>
